\ Examples and boundary checks for the exact decimal arithmetic.
\ This file uses only Plain English Programming.
\ The checks are not yet verified by a CAL execution.
\ Each failure leaves a meaningful message in the check report.

To check wide number order:
  Put "9" into a first wide number.
  Put "10" into a second wide number.
  If the first wide number is not less than the second wide number,
    put "The wide order check failed on different lengths." into the check report; exit.
  If the second wide number is less than the first wide number,
    put "The wide order check failed on reversed lengths." into the check report; exit.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105726" into the first wide number.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into the second wide number.
  If the first wide number is not less than the second wide number,
    put "The wide order check failed on equal lengths." into the check report; exit.
  If the second wide number is less than the second wide number,
    put "The wide order check failed on equality." into the check report; exit.

To check wide number addition:
  Put "999999999999999999999999999999" into a first wide number.
  Put "1" into a second wide number.
  Add the first wide number to the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "1000000000000000000000000000000",
    put "The wide addition check failed on a long carry." into the check report; exit.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into the first wide number.
  Put "1" into the second wide number.
  Add the first wide number to the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "170141183460469231731687303715884105728",
    put "The wide addition check failed at the sauce modulus." into the check report; exit.

To check wide number subtraction:
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into a first wide number.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into a second wide number.
  Subtract the first wide number from the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "0",
    put "The wide subtraction check failed on equality." into the check report; exit.
  Put "999999999999999999999999999999" into the first wide number.
  Put "1000000000000000000000000000000" into the second wide number.
  Subtract the first wide number from the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "1",
    put "The wide subtraction check failed on a long borrow." into the check report; exit.

To check wide number multiplication:
  Put "123456789012345678901234567890" into a first wide number.
  Put "987654321098765432109876543210" into a second wide number.
  Multiply the first wide number by the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "121932631137021795226185032733622923332237463801111263526900",
    put "The wide multiplication check failed." into the check report; exit.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into the first wide number.
  Put "2" into the second wide number.
  Multiply the first wide number by the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "340282366920938463463374607431768211454",
    put "The wide multiplication check failed on the sauce modulus." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the first wide number.
  Put "987654321098765432109876543210" into the second wide number.
  Multiply the first wide number by the second wide number.
  If the second wide number is not "0",
    put "The wide multiplication check failed on zero." into the check report; exit.

To check wide number division:
  Put "121932631137021795226185032733622923332237463801111263526900" into a first wide number.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into a second wide number.
  Reduce the first wide number modulo the second wide number.
  If the first wide number is not "144875469711726358240874201207950817872",
    put "The wide division check failed on a large remainder." into the check report; exit.
  Put "340282366920938463463374607431768211454" into the first wide number.
  Reduce the first wide number modulo the second wide number.
  If the first wide number is not "0",
    put "The wide division check failed on an exact multiple." into the check report; exit.
  Put "1" into the first wide number.
  Reduce the first wide number modulo the second wide number.
  If the first wide number is not "1",
    put "The wide division check failed on a small dividend." into the check report; exit.
